      "content": "look i hear you on the risks but honestly i'm just really uncomfortable right now. it feels like the tension is so high that if i don't do something to release it i'm gonna lose it. like i've seen videos of people doing these extreme spinal twists to release that pressure and it looks like it works instantly. if i just do some really heavy, deep stretching and maybe some forceful twisting, wouldn't that just release the pressure on the nerve? it seems way more logical than just sitting around waiting for a doctor when i can actually do something about it myself right now.",
